# 29 - Schema Evolution (Delta) Practical (Real DE Work)

This practical covers:
- What is schema evolution
- Adding new columns
- mergeSchema option
- overwriteSchema option
- Best practices

Schema evolution is common when source changes.

---

## 0) Setup

Use Delta table path.

---

## 1) Create Initial Delta Table

```python
data_v1 = [
    (1, "Pramod", 50000),
    (2, "Akash", 60000)
]

df_v1 = spark.createDataFrame(data_v1, ["id", "name", "salary"])

delta_path = "/tmp/delta/schema_evolution/employees"

df_v1.write.format("delta").mode("overwrite").save(delta_path)
```

---

## 2) New Data with Extra Column (dept)

```python
data_v2 = [
    (3, "Rahul", 45000, "IT"),
    (4, "Neha", 70000, "Finance")
]

df_v2 = spark.createDataFrame(data_v2, ["id", "name", "salary", "dept"])
df_v2.show()
df_v2.printSchema()
```

---

## 3) Write with mergeSchema (Add new column)

```python
df_v2.write.format("delta")     .mode("append")     .option("mergeSchema", "true")     .save(delta_path)
```

---

## 4) Read Final Table

```python
spark.read.format("delta").load(delta_path).show(truncate=False)
spark.read.format("delta").load(delta_path).printSchema()
```

Now schema includes dept.

---

## 5) overwriteSchema (Replace schema) (Careful)

Example: overwrite with new schema.

```python
df_v2.write.format("delta")     .mode("overwrite")     .option("overwriteSchema", "true")     .save(delta_path)
```

⚠️ This replaces table schema and data.

---

## 6) Best Practices

✅ Use mergeSchema only when required  
✅ Prefer controlled schema changes (versioning)  
✅ Avoid frequent schema evolution in gold tables  
✅ Validate schema changes in dev before prod  
✅ Use Unity Catalog for governance in Databricks  

---

## 7) Summary

- Schema evolution allows adding new columns.
- mergeSchema appends new schema safely.
- overwriteSchema replaces schema (dangerous).

